You are the INTERIOR DESIGNER of the storeroom SW: Store room: barrels along the outer walls, one lamp, plain floor.. Its inner air is the box [1,2,42,10,5,46] (x0,y0,z0,x1,y1,z1); it is entered through door (10, 2..3, 41) to the peristyle south walkway. Design it for its purpose and build it, inside that box only: a layout that reads at a glance (a focal piece, furniture grouped by use), real blocks with correct states (stairs as seats, slabs and trapdoors as tables and shelves, beds with facing and part, barrels, lanterns, carpets, flower pots, item frames are not blocks), light so it isn't dark, nothing over the doorways or windows. Keep it WALKABLE: a 2-high clear path from every way in across the room and up to every bed, table and workstation; check with `$MCD walk build.nbt --rooms rooms.json` that your room reads ok.
